      "message": "qa: check the timeouts of Sock::Wait() and Sock::WaitMany()\n\nWithout events, a wait returns true once its timeout expires and reports\nnothing, also when a socket on which nothing is requested is readable.\nCallers rely on it to pace their loops (net.cpp, httpserver.cpp) and to\ndetect a timeout (ConnectToSocket() in netbase.cpp, i2p.cpp, pcp.cpp).\n\nA negative timeout is not tested: poll() would wait forever and select()\nfails. No caller passes one.\n\nRemove the wait test: it exercises strictly less than the long_timeout\ntest introduced in this commit.",
