      "message": "qa: pin down the options of CreateSockOS() and accepted sockets\n\nCheck that CreateSockOS() sockets are non-blocking and have TCP_NODELAY\nand, where it exists, SO_NOSIGPIPE, and which of these a socket accepted\nfrom one inherits.\n\nnet.cpp and httpserver.cpp do not make accepted sockets non-blocking.\nOn Linux they are not, as accept() does not pass O_NONBLOCK on, and the\ncallers rely on MSG_DONTWAIT instead. Check that Recv() and Send() with\nMSG_DONTWAIT return would-block rather than wait on a socket as accept()\nreturns it. Where MSG_DONTWAIT does not exist (Windows), check at compile\ntime that accepted sockets inherit non-blocking mode, and at run time\nthat they do.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Antoine Poinsot",
        "email": "mail@antoinep.com",
        "date": "2026-11-02T22:40:02Z"
